Quoting  James  <james.kanze@gmail.com>:
>Traps don't depend on your level, only on the level in the
>dungeon.  Level 8 and below can have a polymorph trap even if
>you're XP1.  (I think they can occur even higher in a bones
>level in the mines.) 

When you are in the endgame, level_difficulty() is the average of the
sanctum's depth and your XL. Of course this makes no difference to traps,
since that number is high enough to permit any trap and trap generation in
the endgame is peculiar anyway; but it does mean that monster difficulty
in the endgame, which uses the average of XL and level_difficulty(), is
weighted 3 times as strongly to XL as to the Sanctum's depth. I wonder if
that means that the conventional wisdom, that low XL cannot prevent
Archons and other nasties in the endgame, is wrong?
